  "branch": "methods",
  "abstract": "Radiocarbon and zircon U–Pb are accepted clocks; this paper targets sample-level accuracy instead. Both share one failure: foreign older material biases ages old, differing only in detectability—homogeneous and hidden in radiocarbon, granular and separable in zircon. One protocol meets it on both: screen, classify on age-independent grounds, correct where characterisable, cross-check, and report honest uncertainty, validated out-of-sample on real radiocarbon, Lava Creek, and open zircon data.",
